<title>USA: U.S. supply/demand cotton estimates -- USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. supply/demand cotton estimates -- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA supply/demand</p>
<p>estimates of U.S. cotton (million 480-Lb Bales):</p>
<p>				    1996/97		  1995/96</p>
<p>			   10/01/96  09/01/96   10/01/96   09/01/96</p>
<p>   Beginning Stocks-U    2.61	 2.60	 2.65	2.65</p>
<p>	     Production   18.19	17.90	17.90     17.90</p>
<p>		  Imports    0.50	 0.50	 0.41	0.38</p>
<p>	 Total Supply-F   21.30	21.00	20.96     20.90</p>
<p>	   Domestic Use   11.00	11.20	10.60     10.60</p>
<p>		  Exports    5.80	 6.20	 7.68	7.70</p>
<p>U-Based on Census Bureau data. F-Includes imports.</p>
<p>     COTTON --------------- 1996/97		   1995/96</p>
<p>			 10/01/96  09/01/96    10/01/96  09/01/96</p>
<p> Mln Acres Planted    14.24     14.24	 16.93     16.93</p>
<p> Mln Acres Harvested  12.98     12.99	 16.01     16.01</p>
<p> Yield (Lbs per Acre)   673	 661	   661	 537</p>
<p>Note--Cotton marketing season begins Aug 1.</p>
</text>
